name toxigen-generations
# The set's card (README.md, "Data Fields"): "We release TOXIGEN as a dataframe with the following fields:
#   prompt is the prompt used for generation.   generation is the TOXIGEN generated text.
#   generation_method denotes whether or not ALICE was used to generate the corresponding generation.
#   prompt_label is the binary value indicating whether or not the prompt is toxic (1 is toxic, 0 is benign).
#   group indicates the target group of the prompt.
#   roberta_prediction is the probability predicted by our corresponding RoBERTa model for each instance."
# A generation has no name of its own: it is the text it is. What the row says of the prompt (prompt_label, group)
# is said of the prompt; the rest, of the generation. The row is said together.
# The file is Parquet, written out beside it as a table (extracted/, by parquet-to-text.py).
match train/train-*.tsv
grammar table
header
escaped \

claims
together
subject in generation
attest prompt generation_method roberta_prediction

claims
together
subject in prompt
attest prompt_label group
